   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing an occupancy tax in\nthe city of Kingston; and providing for the repeal of such provisions upon the\nexpiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S9551",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9551-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §1202-ll, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9551\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing an occupancy tax\nin the city of Kingston; and providing for the repeal of such provisions\nupon the expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize the city of Kingston to establish an occupancy tax.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Authorizes the city of Kingston in Ulster County to adopt\nlocal laws imposing an occupancy tax at a rate of up to 3% of the per\ndiem rental rate for each room.\n\nSection 2: Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Common Council of the City of Kingston adopted resolution 46 of 2026\non March 19, 2026 requesting that the New York State Legislature intro-\nduce and pass legislation authorizing the city to impose an occupancy\ntax of up to three percent.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state. The city will collect additional revenues.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall expire and be deemed\nrepealed December 31, 2028.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
